  "conventions_note": "DELIVERABLE 2, GDN2's side: the recipe-correct comparison arm at the machine-seed pairing of the banked best row (3401)",
  "no_prediction": {
    "rule": "NO DIRECTIONAL PREDICTION is pre-stated for any arm: the literature does not say which machine benefits more from the corrected instrument or from the Moonlight LR point -- the gate-surface difference (our 27.7K learned gate params vs GDN2's 27.4M) makes both directions live; this lane measures, and any reversal is reported as plainly as any confirmation"
  },
  "corrected_scoring": {
    "primary": "post-cooldown eval: a linear cooldown of 24 steps (13.3% of the 180-step constant-LR budget) appended after the banked matched-exposure landing, same stream/data order, LR factor (25 - k)/24 for cooldown step k (1.0 -> 1/24, never zero), both hybrid groups scaling equally; the corrected score is the post-cooldown calibration eval",
    "secondary": "EMA iterate at step 180 (no extra data): decay 0.99, initialized at the init weights, updated after every constant-phase optimizer step, NOT updated during the cooldown; RANKING-ONLY -- its absolute number is biased toward mid-run weights (stated, not smoothed)",
    "cooldown_steps": 24,
    "cooldown_fraction": 0.1333,
    "cooldown_form": "linear",
    "ema_decay": 0.99,
    "exposure_note": "the cooldown steps see ~2.7M more targets (~13%), identical across arms -- a stated protocol EXTENSION; the step-180 constant-LR eval is retained so every banked row stays comparable",
    "citations": {
      "river_valley": "Wen et al., ICLR 2025, arXiv:2410.05192 -- constant-LR loss carries an LR-dependent oscillation penalty that decay/averaging removes",
      "cooldown": "Haegele et al., NeurIPS 2024, arXiv:2405.18392 -- constant-LR + short cooldown matches cosine at full scale",
      "averaging": "Defazio et al., arXiv:2405.15682 -- iterate averaging as the schedule-free fix for the same penalty",
      "moonlight": "Liu et al. (Moonshot AI), arXiv:2502.16982 -- with the update RMS matched to AdamW's (~0.2; AdamW typical 0.2-0.4), Muon directly reuses the LR and weight decay tuned for AdamW, i.e. ~1x the AdamW-tuned LR, WITH weight decay",
      "horizon": "Bjorck et al., ICLR 2025 -- the optimal LR shrinks with token horizon; probe-tuned LRs transfer only downscaled"
    }
  },
